---
/* "It handles the in-between." Five small jobs, each a mock rebuilt from the shipped app:
   1 ios/TracendWidgets/RestLiveActivity.swift, ios/Shared/RestActivityAttributes.swift
   2 lib/features/train/widgets/exercise_detail_sheet.dart, train_parts.dart (next target and why)
   3 lib/features/nutrition/widgets/nutrition_sheets.dart (candidate card, portion chooser, source badge)
   4 lib/features/readiness/pain_check_sheet.dart, safety_copy.dart, day_adjustment_card.dart
   5 lib/features/coach/memory/coach_memory_screen.dart, widgets/fact_suggestion_chip.dart
   The markup is each card's finished state; scripts/extras.js plays a one-shot on top. */
---
<section class="sec wrap" id="extras" aria-labelledby="extras-h">
  <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="extras-h">The small jobs a coach does, done for you.</h2>
  <p class="ex-tag-row"><span class="ex-tag">Example screens</span></p>

  <ul class="ex-rail" role="list" tabindex="0" aria-label="Five things it handles between sessions" data-ex-rail>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="lock">
      <div class="ex-mock app ex-ls" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-ls-wall"><span class="ex-ls-time">9:41</span></div>
        <div class="ex-ls-card">
          <div class="ex-ls-layer ex-ls-set" data-ex-set>
            <div class="ex-ls-row">
              <div class="ex-ls-lab">
                <span class="ex-ls-st"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2"/><path d="M4 9h16M7 9v6M17 9v6M12 9v6M9 21l3-6 3 6"/></svg>Set 4 of 5</span>
                <b class="ex-ls-ex a-num">Back squat</b>
              </div>
              <span class="ex-ls-tgt a-num">120 kg &times; 5</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ex-ls-btns">
              <span class="ex-ls-btn lime" data-ex-log><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3.2 8.4l3 3 6.6-6.8"/></svg>Log set<i class="ex-ripple"></i></span>
              <span class="ex-ls-btn raised">Open</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-ls-layer ex-ls-rest" data-ex-rest>
            <div class="ex-ls-row">
              <div class="ex-ls-lab">
                <span class="ex-ls-st"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="7.5"/><path d="M12 9v4l2.5 1.5M9.5 2.5h5"/></svg>Rest</span>
                <b class="ex-ls-ex a-num">Back squat</b>
                <span class="ex-ls-dt">Next: Set 4 of Back squat</span>
              </div>
              <span class="ex-ls-cd a-num" data-ex-cd>0:00</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ex-ls-btns">
              <span class="ex-ls-btn raised">+30s</span>
              <span class="ex-ls-btn raised"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 3.5l6 4.5-6 4.5zM12.5 3v10"/></svg>Skip</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example Lock Screen card. Set 4 of 5, Back squat, 120 kilograms for 5. The lime Log set button is next to an Open button. During rest, the card shows a countdown with plus 30 seconds and Skip.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Log sets from your Lock Screen.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">A rest timer and the next set wait on your Lock Screen. Tap to log it without opening the app.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="prog">
      <div class="ex-mock app ex-pg" aria-hidden="true">
        <p class="ex-pg-h"><b>Back squat</b><span>Next session</span></p>
        <div class="ex-tiles">
          <div class="ex-tile ex-tile-next" data-ex-tile><span class="k">Next target</span><span class="v a-num"><span class="ex-roll"><span class="o">120</span><span class="n">122.5</span></span> kg &times; 5</span></div>
          <div class="ex-tile"><span class="k">Sets &times; reps</span><span class="v a-num">5 &times; 5</span></div>
          <div class="ex-tile"><span class="k">Rest</span><span class="v a-num">3 min</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="ex-pg-aim">Aim for about 2 to 3 reps left on each set.</p>
        <p class="ex-pg-why" data-ex-why>Every set reached the top of the range last time. Add weight and start the reps again.</p>
        <div class="ex-list">
          <p><span>Last time</span><b class="a-num">120 kg &times; 5, 5, 5, 5, 5</b></p>
          <p><span>Your best</span><b class="a-num">120 kg &times; 5</b></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example exercise screen for the back squat. Last time: 120 kilograms for 5, 5, 5, 5 and 5. Every set reached the top of the range, so the next target is 122.5 kilograms for 5.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">It tells you when to add weight.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Hit the top reps on every set and your next target goes up. Fall short and the weight holds.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="pain">
      <div class="ex-mock app ex-pn" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-pn-in" data-ex-in>
          <p class="ex-pn-q">Where?</p>
          <div class="ex-pn-chips"><span class="on">Knee</span><span>Lower back</span><span>Shoulder</span><span>Somewhere else</span></div>
          <p class="ex-pn-q">How strong right now?</p>
          <div class="ex-pn-sev"><span>1</span><span>2</span><span>3</span><span>4</span><span class="on">5</span><span>6</span><span>7</span><span>8</span><span>9</span><span>10</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-pn-card" data-ex-res>
          <b class="ex-pn-t">Easier on your joints today</b>
          <p class="ex-pn-l"><span class="ex-pn-old">Barbell back squat</span><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M2.5 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg><span class="ex-pn-new">Goblet squat</span></p>
          <p class="ex-pn-s">Only today changes. Your plan stays the same.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example pain check. Where: knee. How strong right now: 5 out of 10. The result reads Easier on your joints today: barbell back squat is swapped for goblet squat. Only today changes and the plan stays the same.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Sore knee? It works around it.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Tell it where it hurts. It swaps or shortens the exercise, and tells you when to see a professional.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="label">
      <div class="ex-mock app ex-lb" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-lb-photo" data-ex-photo>
          <span class="ex-lb-t">Nutrition facts</span>
          <span class="ex-lb-l"><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span class="ex-lb-l"><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span class="ex-lb-l"><i></i><i></i></span>
          <b class="ex-scan" data-ex-scan></b>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-cand" data-ex-cand>
          <div class="ex-cand-row">
            <span class="ex-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3.2 8.4l3 3 6.6-6.8"/></svg></span>
            <span class="ex-cand-t"><b>Protein bar</b><span>1 serving (60 g) &middot; 210 kcal &middot; High confidence</span></span>
          </div>
          <span class="ex-badge" data-ex-badge>From label</span>
          <p class="ex-ask">How much did you eat?</p>
          <div class="ex-seg"><span class="on">1 serving</span><span>Whole pack</span><span>Grams</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example meal review. A photo of a nutrition label becomes one food: Protein bar, 1 serving of 60 grams, 210 calories, marked From label. A portion chooser offers 1 serving, Whole pack or Grams.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Snap the label, not just the plate.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">It reads nutrition labels and checks the math. You pick the portion.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="mem">
      <div class="ex-mock app ex-mm" aria-hidden="true">
        <ul class="ex-facts">
          <li class="due" data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.2"/><path d="M8 4.6V8l2.2 1.4"/></svg><span>Knee pain on deep squats</span></li>
          <li data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 1.6l5.2 2v3.7c0 3.2-2.1 5.6-5.2 7.1-3.1-1.5-5.2-3.9-5.2-7.1V3.6z"/><path d="M5.6 8l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4"/></svg><span>Trains before work</span></li>
          <li data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 1.6l5.2 2v3.7c0 3.2-2.1 5.6-5.2 7.1-3.1-1.5-5.2-3.9-5.2-7.1V3.6z"/><path d="M5.6 8l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4"/></svg><span>Vegetarian</span></li>
          <li data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 1.6l5.2 2v3.7c0 3.2-2.1 5.6-5.2 7.1-3.1-1.5-5.2-3.9-5.2-7.1V3.6z"/><path d="M5.6 8l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4"/></svg><span>Dumbbells at home</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="ex-ask-card" data-ex-ask>
          <p class="ex-ask-h"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M4 2h8v12l-4-3-4 3z"/></svg>Still true?</p>
          <p class="ex-ask-q">&ldquo;Knee pain on deep squats&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="ex-ask-r">You confirmed it on 12 Oct. Is it still true?</p>
          <div class="ex-ask-b"><span>Dismiss</span><span class="lime">Confirm</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example Coach memory. Saved facts: Knee pain on deep squats, Trains before work, Vegetarian, Dumbbells at home. A card asks Still true? about the knee, with Dismiss and Confirm.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">It remembers what you tell it.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Your limits and preferences shape every plan. It checks in later: still true?</p>
    </li>

  </ul>
  <div class="ex-dots" aria-hidden="true" data-ex-dots><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
</section>
